YAAP Sam-Hum-Mal-Law
genocideless, polyselfless, polypileless, artiwishless

My alphabetic ascension series continues with Samurai. Only one game
was needed to win, so now I have open three game streak! Overall,
Samurai is an easy role since it has no problem with killing stuff. I
wanted to use attack spells too, but I was hindered by low
intelligence and metallic armor. Eventually, I used only magic missile
and even that only for things that were dangerous from close range
(mainly green slimes).

1) Did the Mines first; temple in Minetown was coaligned, so I got my
Snickersnee quick; in lower mines I got two luckstones and amulet of
ESP.

2) Sokoban gave me reflection.

3) I got Arc bones with tinning kit and magic lamp.

4) By midgame I was really good at melee -- expert in long sword and
two-weaponing I was hacking monsters with great ease. I decided to go
for genocideless, since I should have minimal problems with master and
arch-liches. This was good decision, since I never found scroll of
genocide anyway.

5) I was bit afraid of Quest, but it was really easy matter. I
paralyzed Ashikaga Takauji with potion and he was at 15 HP after my
first blow. He never even realized I was there. I didn't use the
Tsurugi, but continued two-weaponing Snickersnee and katana, except
for disenchanters.

6) Gehennom mapping done by hand - no means of magic mapping except
for two scrolls. Got another magic lamp in Orcus Town, along with
Orcus' wand (picture perfect kill, Orcus hadn't even woken up).

7) I had to wish for most of ascension kit armor and two magic
markers, since overall the loot was very poor in this game. On the
other hand I had lots of full healings, so I could easily upgrade my
HP to about 300 and still keep 10 potions for the run. I also found
most of the rings I needed (levitation, free action, teleport control
-- no conflict, though).

8) In the Wizard's Tower top level I for the first time in my
nethacking career met and slew Geryon (summoned by a balrog or
something). Also got my third magic lamp there.

9) Moloch's Sanctum was bit tense since I had no conflict and arch-
liches roamed about, but I got the Amulet without serious trouble (and
also obtained athame from one of the purple Ls). I had to walk to
upstairs, since I had no c!oGL, but it wasn't that bad.

10) On the run to planes I had number of Rodney sessions and
mysterious force annoyed me to no end, but all in all it was rather a
breeze, except that I once ran into a disenchanter, so my +7 katana
ended up as +6.

11) Earth was nominal, on Air I meleed three or four elementals
without any trouble. Fire was nominal again, but for Water I switched
to levitation boots and oilskin and removed primary rings -- but it
was completely uneventful and quick matter, surprisingly. I got three
Rodney visitations on the Planes, too.

12) Astral plane was the worst I ever experienced. I planned to wish
for trice corpse, for which reason I brought three magic lamps. In a
stroke of extremely bad luck I got no wish out of them (yes, they were
blessed), thats probability of 0.8%! Instead I got one hostile djinni,
one peaceful djinni and one tame djinni. Well, there was nothing else
to do but fight in honorable combat. First two altars were Death and
Famine and were bit slow going (no conflict) but otherwise no
particular trouble. The third altar was Pestilence. My wand's of death
two last charges missed and Pestilence managed to disease me twice in
a row -- luckily I had full healing out, so I survived and killed him
(or is it her?) in melee. But it was uncomfortably close call.

